:name: CANcestry T2 virtual bench
:description: Bring-up of the STM32G474-class platform model and the v1.0.0 firmware ELF for the HW-SF-002 retention sequence (H-07, issue #53).

# CANcestry T2 virtual bench bring-up script (H-07, issue #53).
#
# Renode platform script (.resc) for the platform described by
# stm32g474-cancestry.repl. The issue text names 'cancestry-hw.cs (or
# equivalent Renode script)'; .resc is Renode's script format and this file
# is that equivalent - no C# peripheral code exists in this repository.
#
# Implements: HW-FR-001 (the v1.0.0 firmware ELF boots and executes on the
# platform model), HW-SF-002 / HW-SF-004 (QA-EV-01 escalation events are
# observable with exact emulation-time timestamps). Governing documents:
# docs/hw/virtual-bench-plan.md sections 1, 3 and 6; HwAGENTS.md rule 5.
#
# The script is driven by the T2 runner (hw/virtual-bench/run_t2_retention.py):
#
#   $elf   path of the v1.0.0 firmware ELF (mandatory; set with
#          `set $elf @...` before including this script - the runner always
#          sets it, and the guard below fails closed when it is missing)
#   $seed  optional deterministic seed (fixed default below; overriding it
#          is a reviewable, evidence-affecting change)
#
# Renode is executed with the working directory set to this file's directory
# so the PythonPeripheral `filename:` attributes resolve; the runner checks
# the pinned Renode version BEFORE including this script (fail-closed).

using sysbus

# Fixed deterministic seed (HwAGENTS.md rule 5).
$t2_seed?="123456789"

# Fail-closed guard: T2 executes the REAL v1.0.0 ELF (HW-PLAN section 8.3);
# the bench never falls back to a reimplementation of the firmware.
python "assert variables['elf'] not in ('', None), 'cancestry-hw.resc: no firmware ELF provided (set $elf before including this script)'"
# F-21/F-22 (issue #55): step markers. Dispatch 9 (run 35726064092) showed
# the t2_trace region (0x60000000) never mapped with no error logged.
# F-22 finding: python print() inside a monitor python command goes to the
# TELNET CLIENT, not to Renode's stdout (MonitorPythonEngine.ConfigureOutput
# redirects stdout to the command interaction writer), so the dispatch 10
# markers were invisible in the console log; Logger.Info goes to the
# console-logged logger instead. The markers (deterministic, console-logged)
# identify the exact step the include reaches; the value-carrying readbacks
# turn the platform state into log evidence. They stay in the script as the
# bring-up audit trail.
python "import Antmicro.Renode.Logging as _clog"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step0: python logger channel OK, elf=%s' % variables['elf'])"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] scope: sysbus=%s machine=%s variables=%s' % ('sysbus' in dir() and 'yes' or 'NO', 'machine' in dir() and 'yes' or 'NO', 'variables' in dir() and 'yes' or 'NO'))"

mach create "cancestry"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step2: machine created')"

# F-24 (issue #55): load the platform file via $ORIGIN - the standard
# Renode idiom. Dispatch 14 (run 35773043927) proved the process CWD is
# /opt/renode (the Renode install dir, step2b probe), so bare names do
# NOT resolve against this script's directory, and the monitor's
# file-not-found path degrades into a URI 'download' attempt and a
# 'Parameters did not match the signature' error (there is no public
# 'Could not find file' line for command path arguments). $ORIGIN is set
# by the include loader (Monitor.TryExecuteScript) to THIS script's
# directory before its lines run, and PathToken trims the '@' prefix -
# so '$ORIGIN/<file>' expands to the clean absolute path of the .repl
# next to this .resc, from any CWD. The original H-07 form
# '@$ORIGIN/<file>' - an EXTRA leading @ on top of the variable's own
# '@' (dispatches 7-11) - and the F-23 bare name (dispatch 14) both
# failed for the reasons above.
python "import os; _o = variables['global.ORIGIN']; _p = (_o.Value if hasattr(_o, 'Value') else str(_o)) + '/stm32g474-cancestry.repl'; _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step2b: repl isfile=%s (%s)' % (os.path.isfile(_p), _p))"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/stm32g474-cancestry.repl
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step3: platform loaded')"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step3b: scope after load: sysbus=%s machine=%s monitor.Machine=%s' % ('sysbus' in dir() and 'yes' or 'NO', 'machine' in dir() and 'yes' or 'NO', 'yes' if monitor.Machine is not None else 'NO'))"

# F-28 (issue #55): register the four scripted register models HERE, with
# $ORIGIN-absolute paths (see the F-28 note in stm32g474-cancestry.repl).
# `machine PyDevFromFile <path> <address> <size> [initable] [name]` is the
# public Machine extension (PythonPeripheralExtensions, v1.16.1) that
# constructs a PythonPeripheral and registers it on the machine's sysbus -
# the same object the previous inline .repl declarations created, minus
# the CWD-relative `filename:` resolution that broke dispatch 17
# (run 35805300102).
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/iwdg_model.py 0x40003000 0x14 true iwdg
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/rtc_backup_model.py 0x40002800 0x64 false rtc_backup
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/gpioa_model.py 0x48000000 0x400 true gpioa
machine PyDevFromFile $ORIGIN/rcc_model.py 0x40021000 0x98 true rcc
python "import os; _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step3c: 4 pydev registered, cwd=%s' % os.getcwd())"

# Deterministic execution (virtual-bench-plan section 6): fixed global
# quantum (100 us master step) and a fixed seed for the only Renode
# randomness source. `emulation RunFor` advances virtual time exactly - no
# wall clock is consumed.
emulation SetGlobalQuantum "0.0001"
emulation SetSeed $t2_seed
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step4: quantum and seed set')"

sysbus LoadELF $elf
# Readback: the initial SP word of the vector table (0x20018000 per
# startup.s) proves the ELF segments reached flash; an unmapped access
# logs a 'non existing peripheral' warning in the console. The bus
# accessor picks whichever scope name the monitor bound (F-23: the
# step3b probe logs which one that is).
python "bus = sysbus if 'sysbus' in dir() else (machine['sysbus'] if 'machine' in dir() else monitor.Machine['sysbus']); v = bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x08000000); _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step5: vector SP=0x%08x (ELF loaded)' % v)"

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# T2 event-capture hooks (HwAGENTS.md rule 5: deterministic, hashed trace).
#
# Each hook stamps the exact emulation virtual time (microseconds) into the
# T2 trace area. The hooks fire on the REAL firmware executing its REAL
# escalation path - nothing in the firmware is modified or reimplemented.
# Slot layout is the platform-file contract (stm32g474-cancestry.repl).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------

cpu AddSymbolHook "cancestry_watchdog_write_retention_register" """
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x60000008, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""

cpu AddSymbolHook "cancestry_hardware_set_safe_state" """
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x6000000C, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""

cpu AddSymbolHook "cancestry_watchdog_escalate" """
machine['sysbus'].WriteDoubleWord(0x60000010, int(round(machine.ElapsedVirtualTime.TimeElapsed.TotalSeconds * 1000000)))
"""
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step6: symbol hooks installed')"

# Trace-area magic: the runner and the FMI bridge refuse to run against a
# machine whose capture area was not initialized by this script.
sysbus WriteDoubleWord 0x60000000 0x54324353
# Readback: 0x54324353 proves the t2_trace region is mapped and writable;
# an unmapped access logs a 'non existing peripheral' warning instead.
python "bus = sysbus if 'sysbus' in dir() else (machine['sysbus'] if 'machine' in dir() else monitor.Machine['sysbus']); v = bus.ReadDoubleWord(0x60000000); _clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step7: t2_trace readback=0x%08x (expected 0x54324353)' % v)"
python "_clog.Logger.Info('[cancestry-hw] step8: include complete, machine left paused')"

# The machine is left PAUSED: the FMI bridge alone advances emulation with
# fixed-size `emulation RunFor` quanta (deterministic co-simulation, no
# free-running). This configuration must NOT be started with `start`.
